# Voice Typing

Moonshine ONNX voice dictation for Linux/Wayland.

## Install

    $ nix profile install .

## Usage

Bind `diktat-toggle` to a key in your Sway config:

    bindsym XF86Favorites exec diktat-toggle

- First press: loads model, then starts recording
- Second press: stops recording, transcribes, types result
- Subsequent presses: instant toggle (model stays loaded)

## How it works

- `diktat-daemon`: background process that keeps the model in RAM
- `diktat-toggle`: starts daemon if needed, toggles recording via signal
- `diktat-repeat`: re-types the last transcription

The daemon stays running for instant recording on subsequent toggles. It auto-shuts
down after 15 minutes idle.

## Updating

The keybinding resolves `diktat-toggle` at each press, so a new build takes
effect on the next press. An already-running daemon keeps the old code in RAM
until it exits, though. To check which build is live:

    $ diktat-daemon -version

This prints the installed store path and the running daemon's, and says so when
they differ. The daemon also logs its own store path on startup.

## Stop daemon manually

    $ pkill -f diktat-daemon
